at of  breast milk flipping the way to casein  i'm not going to get into the deep  science here but it's also like leaving  out ingredients like palm oil which  leads to a lot of constipation and palm  oil is a very common ingredient that you  see in pretty much all u.s formulas you  know the other thing i like about your  story not only do you have such a great  product but i like your back personal  story because you had launched this  company it was going well they did a  piece on you next thing you know fda  agents are showing up at your place with  clipboards you write and you said your  heart  dropped to your stomach never a good  feeling and they not only chose to shut  you down they also issued a recall and  it wasn't because the ingredients were  bad it all had to do with labeling yeah  but laura you did not let that defeat  you that's what i think is so amazing  you did not let that defeat you you  carried on what did you do well  oh well first off hearing you say that  out again it brings all the emotions  back yeah it is such a journey to start  a company right but  there is nothing like being told no to a  group of fiery moms who by the way at  the time i was pregnant saying you know  what no i knew the impact that we could  have on this product is what the u.s  deserved so we kept powering through we  got to get into the shame part of this  that our colleagues  brought up  women feel such pressure to breastfeed  and there's so much shame attached so  much judgment judgment yes  where does that come from well you feel  you have to apologize i remember i would  plan to breastfeed for six months could  only do three and when people ask you  about it it's like you have to apologize  that you didn't make it how do we stop  that shame yes okay  first off no parent and especially a mom  should ever feel guilty about how they  feed their baby period  we did a national survey to find that  two-thirds of parents feel guilty  feeding their babies  two-thirds  and